win32u: Deliver internal IME notifications to the builtin IME window procedure.

post_ime_update() defers composition updates coming from the display driver by
posting WM_WINE_IME_NOTIFY to the focus window; handle_internal_message() then
relays it as WM_IME_NOTIFY(IMN_WINE_SET_COMP_STRING) to the thread's default IME
window through send_message().  That goes through whatever window procedure the
default IME window *currently* has -- and applications are allowed to subclass
it.

MapleStory (Nexon) does exactly that: once its main window is up it replaces the
default IME window's procedure with one that only calls DefWindowProc().  On
Windows this is harmless, because the real IME never routes composition results
through the default IME window.  On Wine it silently drops every composition and
result string: __wine_ime_wnd_proc() -> ime_ui_notify() -> ime_set_comp_string()
-> ImeToAsciiEx() are never reached, so the application never receives
WM_IME_COMPOSITION and nothing typed through XIM/fcitx ever shows up in-game.

Evidence (WINEDEBUG=+imm,+xim on the game): every post_ime_update() is followed
by get_default_ime_window() for the focus window (so the internal message *is*
dequeued and passes the parent check), but __wine_ime_wnd_proc() sees nothing
after WM_ACTIVATEAPP, while DefWindowProc()'s WM_IME_NOTIFY handler runs on the
IME window instead.

This is a Wine-internal notification, so dispatch it to the builtin IME class
procedure directly, the same way NtUserDispatchMessage() dispatches to an
explicit callback.  The default IME window belongs to the current thread, so a
direct dispatch is safe.

--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -2158,9 +2158,14 @@ static LRESULT handle_internal_message( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam )
         return FALSE;
     case WM_WINE_IME_NOTIFY:
     {
+        struct win_proc_params params = {.func = BUILTIN_WINPROC( NTUSER_WNDPROC_IME )};
         HWND ime_hwnd = get_default_ime_window( hwnd );
         if (!ime_hwnd || ime_hwnd == NtUserGetParent( hwnd )) return 0;
-        return send_message( ime_hwnd, WM_IME_NOTIFY, wparam, lparam );
+        /* The application may have subclassed the default IME window (MapleStory does, and its
+         * procedure never forwards to the original one).  This is a Wine-internal notification,
+         * so bypass the window's current procedure and call the builtin IME one directly. */
+        if (!init_win_proc_params( &params, ime_hwnd, WM_IME_NOTIFY, wparam, lparam, FALSE )) return 0;
+        return dispatch_win_proc_params( &params, sizeof(params), NULL, NULL );
     }
     case WM_WINE_WINDOW_STATE_CHANGED:
     {
